# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — 2026-10-23 19:39:45 UTC

Base revision: `a2eb40c2` on `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`.
This record documents a narrow P18-V01 inbound remoting correction.

## P18-V01 finding

- Pinned RocketMQ 5.5.1 `NettyRemotingAbstract.java` source SHA-256:
  `f4c5daa4a9a560df4bf92c5b8d0e058accc54a84ef491e530559280ef0457d7e`.
  `processRequestCommand` first resolves a specific/default processor. If one
  exists and `isShuttingDown` is true, requests newer than
  `MQVersion.Version.V5_3_1.ordinal()` receive `GO_AWAY` (1500, `please go
  away`) before `rejectRequest()` or executor submission. Unsupported request
  codes remain ahead of this check.
- Pinned `MQVersion.java` source SHA-256:
  `8b9a6a4b728f6b74d41f8ab19aac5cb5a39665cd0c05bf227ccba8d571ae5f82`;
  `V5_3_1` is ordinal 475.
- Rust `process_one` applies that cutoff after processor lookup and before
  rejection. The Java fixture invokes four cases: shutdown at 475, shutdown at
  476, running at 476, and unsupported code during shutdown. It records
  response code/remark/opaque and reject/processor counts. Rust tests check the
  boundary response and dispatch ordering.

## Verification

- `cargo test --workspace --locked --quiet` — passed sequentially.
- `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked --quiet` — passed
  sequentially.
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D
  warnings` — passed.
- Windows GNU all-target/all-feature workspace check and strict Clippy —
  passed as compile-only evidence.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — passed.
- Dedicated offline Java fixture verification passed:
  `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml exec:java -Dexec.args='runtime-remoting-shutdown-fixtures fixtures/runtime/remoting-shutdown.json --verify'`.
- Full `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` did not complete.
  The existing `ConsumerLifecycleFixtures.failedLitePullMetadataSchedule`
  case invoked Java's default NameServer address lookup and blocked in DNS.
  The process was stopped after the shutdown fixture and preceding fixture
  executions passed; no shutdown fixture failure was reported.

## Remaining scope

This closes the inbound shutdown version-gate discrepancy only. Broad P18-V01
source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow and reverse-export reconciliation
remains PARTIAL. Native Windows runtime, current-revision remote CI, and Phase
19 live Broker/Docker scenarios were not run. No plan was edited, no push or
remote CI was run, and the four pre-existing Phase 19 worktree paths remain
